<h1><span lang="EN-GB">Rectangular Selection</span></h1>
<hr align="left" width="98.974%" size="6" class="whs3">
<p><span lang="EN-GB">This command is accessible from</span> <span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Select &gt; Region &gt; Rectangle</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">or from the</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>toolbar</b></span><span lang="EN-GB">. If</span> <span class="Button">Rectangular Selection</span> <span lang="EN-GB">is not selected on the toolbar, hold down the left mouse button on the current selection for a second to show up the drop-down toolbar. Select</span> <span class="Button">Rectangular selection</span> <span lang="EN-GB">button from there.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">When</span> <span class="Mode">Rectangular Selection</span> <span lang="EN-GB">mode is selected, press on the toolbar button to activate it.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="Commands_files/image270.gif" width="32px" height="32px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt="">Mouse pointer in</span> <span class="Mode">Rectangular Selection</span> <span lang="EN-GB">mode</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">Then use the left mouse button to draw a rectangle on the objects in the</span> <u><span lang="EN-GB"><a href="../User_Interface/Viewport.htm">viewport</a></span></u><span lang="EN-GB">.</span> Note that the location from where you start is the top left corner of the rectangle, then move <span lang="EN-GB">the mouse to expand it in both directions. When use</span> <span class="Command">Rectangular Selection</span><span lang="EN-GB">, all currently selected areas will be deselected.</span></p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">To add Rectangular selection to the current one h</span>old down the <span class="Shortcut">Ctrl</span> key while moving the mouse.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet">To exclude <span lang="EN-GB">Rectangular</span> selection from the existing one, hold down the <span class="Shortcut">Alt</span> key while moving the mouse.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet">To make square selection, hold down the <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Shift</b></span> key after start moving the mouse.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">T</span>he <span class="Mode">Rectangular Selection</span> mode will remain active until you switch to another mode.</p>
<p class="description"><span lang="EN-GB" class="Command" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">The selection will consist of all visible points and whole visible entities that are inside. Compound entities (like scan data, meshes, point clouds, polylines, etc.) can be selected partially or wholly, depending on what amount of them is covered by the rectangle that is drawn. Datum points and lines must be inside in order to be selected. Centres of datum planes, datum circles, and datum spheres as well as axes of datum cylinders is enough to be inside in order to be selected.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">This mode is not stored so next time when you run KUBE,</span> <span class="Mode">Polygonal Selection</span> <span lang="EN-GB">will be selected automatically.</span></p>
<p class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-GB"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a1" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example</a></span></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP961546712" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p><img src="Images/rectangular_selection.gif" width="188px" height="250px" border="0" class="img_whs5" alt=""></p>
</div>
<p class="Use"><span class="Command">Rectangular Selection</span> <span lang="EN-GB">is mainly</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>used</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">for selecting rectangular areas.</span></p>
